# What goes in /srv/macro-atlas/env/production.env and /srv/macro-atlas/env/staging.env on the
# server (mode 600, owned by the user that runs the timers). It is the environment of the
# ingest container and of nothing else: the web app never sees it. Plain NAME=value lines, no
# quotes, no `export`. Never commit the real file and never paste a key into a chat or a log.
#
# The two free API keys (D8). Without one its source is not asked: the run says STALE for
# each of its endpoints and ends red (deploy/capture/README.md, "API keys").
BEA_API_KEY=
EIA_API_KEY=
# The rights-register rows this host asks, separated by spaces. Empty means every row that
# lists endpoints, and one unsigned row then fails the whole capture. It selects among rows
# and clears none. As signed on 2026-11-12:
ATLAS_CAPTURE_ONLY=bls treasury-fiscal-data fed-board bea eia census
# So an agency can reach a person. Without it the job sends a generic name and no contact.
ATLAS_CAPTURE_USER_AGENT=
